# Deny-list for the publication guard (npm run guard).
#
# Copy this file to .denyterms and replace the placeholders with the real
# terms. .denyterms is git-ignored on purpose: committing the forbidden
# strings would itself publish them, and would make the guard flag its own
# configuration.
#
# One extended-regex pattern per line. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
# Matching is case-insensitive.

# --- Organisation and product names ---
# acme
# acme-internal-product-name

# --- Internal hostnames and registries ---
# [a-z0-9-]+\.acme\.net
# nexus\.acme\.

# --- Namespace URIs and schema/service codes ---
# https?://(www\.)?acme\.com/
# \b[A-Z]{2}[0-9]{4}\b

# --- Distinctive internal field vocabulary ---
# Terms that are unusual enough to fingerprint the source system even with
# every other name removed. These matter more than the obvious ones.
# some_internal_field_name

# --- Personal identifiers ---
# firstname\.lastname@
